    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup optimized to exploit vulnerabilities in several matchups, headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who leads our position players with a 74.56 efficiency score. Facing Bieber, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable 5.25 xERA matchup and a robust +14% platoon edge, making him our primary engine today. **Drake Baldwin** (68.29) and **Jacob Wilson** (65.27) follow closely, both boosted by high-leverage spots in the top of the order and favorable park factors. We are specifically leaning into **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Jacob Wilson** against shaky right-handed arms, as their combined profile provides the best ceiling for our 5x5 Roto needs.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jackson Merrill** on the bench. Despite his 50.88 score, his effectiveness is stifled by a difficult matchup against Williams (2.90 xERA), pushing him below our internal efficiency threshold compared to the high-upside starts of **Andy Pages** (62.64) and **Kyle Tucker** (64.91). While **Jackson Merrill** is a frequent contributor, his projected struggles against a suppressed strikeout environment tipped the optimizer toward alternatives. We also remain vigilant regarding the risk associated with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** against Matz; while both maintain solid scores, their platoon disadvantage against the lefty is partially offset by the slow delivery of the opposition, which theoretically enhances their stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given the extreme scarcity of SB in this format.\n\nWarning flags persist regarding the high-end talent we are facing, specifically Cole and the sub-3.00 xERA arms suppressing the output of players like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.98). While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** maintains a respectable score due to an elite BvP history, we are managing game caps closely, which is why **Luis Lara** remains sidelined with a sub-40 efficiency rating. We will monitor the weather and official lineups for **Wade Meckler** and **Nasim Nunez**, as their utility depends on maintaining their current projected spots in the batting order to sustain their value in an otherwise tight Roto race.",
